WEBVTT

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:07.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday 19 November. Can you all hear me on this thing?</v>

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:14.419
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, loud and clear. Anyone watch the football last night? Honestly, ninety minutes I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.280
<v Callum Reid>You say that every week, though. Still watch it.</v>

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:26.219
<v David Whitfield>More entertaining than sitting here discussing the heating in the portakabin. It's either tropical or absolutely Baltic.</v>

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:29.989
<v Olumide Adeyemi>You've still got your coat on. That answers that.</v>

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the weather forecast. What's finished, then what's actually on the list?</v>

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:43.990
<v Hannah Price>I tested the Injection Moulding Line 3 yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, nothing further off that test.</v>

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:49.539
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. So that's a proper done, not a nearly done?</v>

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.170
<v Hannah Price>A proper done. You're allowed to have one occasionally.</v>

00:00:55.689 --> 00:01:02.689
<v Sarah Okafor>And I signed off the inspection on the palletiser on Tuesday. That's closed as well; not another inspection for today.</v>

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:10.799
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, separate bit of maintenance: I'll grease and check the bearings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel on Friday.</v>

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.150
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Callum. On Friday for that, then.</v>

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.230
<v Callum Reid>Yep, I'll do both, grease and bearing check.</v>

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:27.079
<v David Whitfield>Nice to hear the full name. Usually it's just 'that bit over there' with someone pointing off camera.</v>

00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:34.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you sort the training records for the new starters tomorrow at 9:30? Low priority.</v>

00:01:35.019 --> 00:01:37.120
<v Jamie Brennan>Tomorrow at 9:30, rather than today?</v>

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:45.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, tomorrow at 9:30. It's low priority, not something to drag everything else out of the way for.</v>

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:50.400
<v Jamie Brennan>Fine, I'll sort the training records for the new starters then.</v>

00:01:52.379 --> 00:01:59.379
<v Jamie Brennan>While I'm on, still waiting on parts for the line 1 mould temp. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.829
<v Callum Reid>Right, that's still blocked, not work we're pretending we can get through today.</v>

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.990
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Also, heard a slight rattle from the Cooling Tower, nothing to action yet. Just an observation.</v>

00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:16.500
<v David Whitfield>Could have been my teeth chattering from in here.</v>

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Very good. Observation only, no action off that.</v>

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:28.090
<v Sarah Okafor>Marc, can you run a function test on the Compressed Air Dryer this morning? Top priority please.</v>

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:33.729
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll run the function test this morning. Top of my list.</v>

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.830
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you—function test only? Not rolling the sensor recalibration into that?</v>

00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:47.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Separate jobs. Marcus Hale, can you recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer on Monday? That one's normal priority.</v>

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:55.789
<v Marcus Hale>Full name, blimey. Yes, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer on Monday, normal priority.</v>

00:02:56.129 --> 00:02:59.629
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Okay, so the recalibration isn't being pulled into this morning.</v>

00:03:01.479 --> 00:03:04.979
<v Marcus Hale>No. Function test this morning, recalibration Monday. Two separate bits.</v>

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:13.000
<v Sarah Okafor>And Marc, can you run the monthly fire alarm test today at 2pm? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.639
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test today at 2pm. Got that.</v>

00:03:22.139 --> 00:03:27.039
<v David Whitfield>The bit of the day when you discover how loud your headset really is.</v>

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:38.729
<v Hannah Price>Oh, on alarms—we were going to replace the belt on the Fire Alarm Panel but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it. That's off today's list.</v>

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, leave that cancelled item out. Doesn't change the monthly test.</v>

00:03:44.789 --> 00:03:52.840
<v Olumide Adeyemi>My other status is unchanged: can't get to the stretch wrapper until production gives us a window. Still blocked, not starting it today.</v>

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:58.889
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, there's no window agreed. Nothing new to promise on that in this meeting.</v>

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.830
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Fair enough. Just didn't want the silence to sound like it was finished.</v>

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:10.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Next one, Marc, can you schedule downtime for the GT1 compressor with production? Normal priority.</v>

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:20.350
<v Marcus Hale>I can't take that one as well, sorry. With the test work already agreed, the scheduling needs to go to someone else.</v>

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:28.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Jamie, can you take over scheduling downtime for the GT1 compressor with production instead? Still normal priority.</v>

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:35.189
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take that over. I'll schedule downtime for the GT1 compressor with production.</v>

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:43.399
<v Callum Reid>Just so we're not bundling things together there—that's arranging the downtime, not owning the permit and isolation as well?</v>

00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:50.089
<v Jamie Brennan>Correct, just the downtime scheduling. I'm not taking the permit or isolation with it.</v>

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:59.379
<v David Whitfield>Which does still need doing: sort the permit to work and isolation for the GT1 compressor this morning. That's a separate gap.</v>

00:05:01.509 --> 00:05:07.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, normal priority for that, due this morning. Anyone able to take the permit to work and isolation?</v>

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.550
<v Marcus Hale>Not me. I can't accept that alongside the Compressed Air Dryer function test.</v>

00:05:14.949 --> 00:05:18.100
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I can't take ownership of that one either, sorry.</v>

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:27.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, no owner for the GT1 compressor permit to work and isolation. It still needs doing this morning, normal priority, but it's unclaimed.</v>

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:37.449
<v Hannah Price>And the other gap: we need to write up the near miss at the palletizer. That's not covered by the inspection sign-off.</v>

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, normal priority for the write-up. Anyone taking it?</v>

00:05:43.329 --> 00:05:45.430
<v Callum Reid>I can't take that one, sorry.</v>

00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:51.160
<v Hannah Price>I haven't got capacity to own it either. I'm flagging the gap, not volunteering.</v>

00:05:51.819 --> 00:05:55.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, the near miss write-up stays unassigned. Nobody's taken it.</v>

00:05:57.579 --> 00:06:04.230
<v David Whitfield>That's the distinction I wanted. Inspection's already done; the account of the near miss isn't. Not another physical inspection.</v>

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.160
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. No repeat inspection being added.</v>

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:16.699
<v Jamie Brennan>That was worth saying. These calls can make one thing sound like three things if the audio drops in the wrong place.</v>

00:06:18.459 --> 00:06:22.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Or if everyone talks at once, which obviously we never do.</v>

00:06:24.779 --> 00:06:25.980
<v Callum Reid>No, we're incredibly—</v>

00:06:28.379 --> 00:06:29.779
<v David Whitfield>—disciplined. Sorry. Couldn't resist.</v>

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:39.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we're clear on what's accepted and what's still got no owner. I'm not counting silence as someone taking those gaps.</v>

00:06:40.189 --> 00:06:41.939
<v Marcus Hale>Yep. All clear from me.</v>

00:06:43.709 --> 00:06:47.910
<v Hannah Price>Same here. Finished items and the pushed-back belt replacement aren't new work.</v>

00:06:48.819 --> 00:06:50.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's us, then. Thanks, everyone.</v>
